@startuml
!include style.puml

title PWasm Persistence Backend: Current Class Structure
caption External research note; update caption with Wizard Engine commit hash/date.

package "Portable API" {
  class BackendRegion {
    +range: Range<byte>
    +backend: TxnRegionBackend
    +markDirty(offset: u64, size: u64): bool
    +persistChanges(): bool
    +persistRange(offset: u64, size: u64): bool
  }

  abstract class TxnRegionBackend {
    +create(size: u64, prot: int): BackendRegion
    +destroy(region: BackendRegion)
    +markDirty(region: BackendRegion, offset: u64, size: u64): bool
    +persistChanges(region: BackendRegion): bool
    +persistRange(region: BackendRegion, offset: u64, size: u64): bool
    +isPersistent(): bool
    +name(): string
  }

  class VolatileBackend
}

package "x86-64 mmap implementation" {
  class FdMmapRegion {
    +mapping: Mapping
    +fd: int
  }

  class FileMmapRegion {
    +hasDirtyChanges: bool
  }

  class PmemMmapRegion {
    +hasPendingWriteback: bool
  }

  abstract class MmapTxnRegionBackend {
    +destroy(region: BackendRegion)
    +validRange(region: BackendRegion, offset: u64, size: u64): bool
    +asFdRegion(region: BackendRegion): FdMmapRegion
    +closeFdRegion(region: BackendRegion)
  }

  class PmemMmapBackend
  class FileMmapBackend
}

BackendRegion --> TxnRegionBackend : delegates to

TxnRegionBackend <|-- VolatileBackend
TxnRegionBackend <|-- MmapTxnRegionBackend
MmapTxnRegionBackend <|-- PmemMmapBackend
MmapTxnRegionBackend <|-- FileMmapBackend

BackendRegion <|-- FdMmapRegion
FdMmapRegion <|-- FileMmapRegion
FdMmapRegion <|-- PmemMmapRegion

PmemMmapBackend ..> PmemMmapRegion : downcasts
FileMmapBackend ..> FileMmapRegion : downcasts

note right of TxnRegionBackend
Design question:
Should the backend interface own all region operations,
or should region objects become typed capabilities?
end note

note bottom of PmemMmapBackend
PMEM path:
markDirty flushes cache lines;
persistChanges issues the fence;
persistRange flushes and fences immediately.
end note

note bottom of FileMmapBackend
File mmap path:
markDirty records dirty state;
persistChanges calls fdatasync;
persistRange calls msync.
end note

@enduml
